1
00:01:55,646 --> 00:02:03,396
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,474 --> 00:02:08,473
No living creature was harmed
during the filming.

3
00:02:11,836 --> 00:02:14,326
My wives...

4
00:02:14,842 --> 00:02:18,842
who devoted themselves to
Kızıl Elma...

5
00:02:20,454 --> 00:02:23,084
and risk their lives
when needed.

6
00:02:26,654 --> 00:02:29,524
My brother.

7
00:02:30,472 --> 00:02:33,582
We overcome all the schemes
of the heathens.

8
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:38,260
All the weapons they drew,
cut them first.

9
00:02:38,901 --> 00:02:43,951
Thank Allah, we have the children,
the future of our tribe.

10
00:02:44,217 --> 00:02:49,147
And the ones who attempted to burn
Söğüt are burned to ashes.

11
00:02:49,963 --> 00:02:53,543
We hit them with the move
they made against us.

12
00:02:54,471 --> 00:02:57,441
Now, it's our turn.

13
00:02:57,643 --> 00:03:00,193
Now is the time for conquest.

14
00:03:00,223 --> 00:03:04,223
Our first objective is İnegöl!

15
00:03:07,517 --> 00:03:12,547
To break those walls down,
we need catapults.

16
00:03:12,783 --> 00:03:16,783
And we need weapons to arm
our alps.

17
00:03:17,998 --> 00:03:21,148
And for that, we need iron.

18
00:03:23,795 --> 00:03:27,185
The way to the castle is full
of mines.

19
00:03:27,475 --> 00:03:30,425
There are iron mines in İnegöl.

20
00:03:32,385 --> 00:03:37,585
If we take it, then we'll solve
our problem.

21
00:03:38,875 --> 00:03:42,025
We need to calculate it, Osman Bey.

22
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:45,950
Are the mines effective?
How many men are protecting them?

23
00:03:46,103 --> 00:03:49,103
The iron is known by
the smith, brother.

24
00:03:49,335 --> 00:03:53,335
Master Davud is already in İnegöl
in disguise.

25
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,950
Mashallah. It's a good move, Osman Bey.
Wise one.

26
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:05,960
-Inshallah, he'll return with good news.
-Inshallah.

27
00:04:07,961 --> 00:04:10,021
Inshallah, he'll return.

28
00:04:12,131 --> 00:04:16,130
Governor Saguros left İznik to
meet us.

29
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:21,130
We'll host him according to
the Turkish customs.

30
00:04:22,233 --> 00:04:25,423
-Are the preparations done?
-Everything is ready, my bey.

31
00:04:25,869 --> 00:04:29,539
İznik will talk about our
hospitality for days, my bey.

32
00:04:29,915 --> 00:04:34,595
We show our hospitality to
those who come as friends.

33
00:04:36,323 --> 00:04:41,493
And we teach the ones who come
as enemies on the battlefield.

34
00:04:43,834 --> 00:04:46,984
Now, sharpen your swords.

35
00:04:48,649 --> 00:04:51,269
The time for conquest is soon.

36
00:05:09,739 --> 00:05:14,159
New miners are coming.
We'll infiltrate with them.

37
00:05:14,724 --> 00:05:18,274
Blend with the crowd.
Don't get attention.

38
00:05:18,551 --> 00:05:21,421
I don't want trouble, alps.

39
00:05:21,616 --> 00:05:24,676
We'll infiltrate, Master Davud.

40
00:05:25,126 --> 00:05:26,686
Come on!

41
00:06:02,152 --> 00:06:05,402
They even stop the villagers
passing through.

42
00:06:06,404 --> 00:06:09,694
The heathens are protecting it well.

43
00:06:21,414 --> 00:06:23,204
Go on.

44
00:07:09,635 --> 00:07:13,515
It's the same on the rear.

45
00:07:14,383 --> 00:07:18,383
It's full of archers.
They chose a good position.

46
00:07:18,737 --> 00:07:20,667
They protect it.

47
00:07:32,417 --> 00:07:36,077
They are here. Scouting first,
conquest later.

48
00:07:36,421 --> 00:07:40,421
Come on, alps.
May Allah help us.

49
00:08:43,294 --> 00:08:45,165
Move, move!

50
00:08:49,433 --> 00:08:51,143
Move!

51
00:09:01,579 --> 00:09:03,139
Move!

52
00:09:09,561 --> 00:09:13,191
-It's Marcus.
-He doesn't know us.

53
00:09:16,245 --> 00:09:18,465
If he does, we are dead.

54
00:09:18,774 --> 00:09:20,944
But we are taking him with us.

55
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:24,770
The end is martyrdom.

56
00:09:27,861 --> 00:09:30,591
What are you talking about there?
Move!

57
00:09:38,346 --> 00:09:39,446
Move!

58
00:09:44,699 --> 00:09:46,939
Move! Move!

59
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:08,347
Do you really consider marrying
Nikola, my lady?

60
00:10:08,830 --> 00:10:10,880
This marriage won't happen, Cornelia.

61
00:10:14,556 --> 00:10:16,746
Love is as strong as death.

62
00:10:17,223 --> 00:10:21,223
How different is spending a life
with someone you don't love than dying?

63
00:10:22,844 --> 00:10:25,014
I will never marry him.

64
00:10:44,416 --> 00:10:47,406
You didn't forget what we talked
about, right?

65
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:51,900
You need to finish your preperations
for marriage.

66
00:10:55,942 --> 00:11:00,582
By the way, you left the castle
yesterday without telling me.

67
00:11:02,804 --> 00:11:05,604
Where did you go?

68
00:11:05,846 --> 00:11:07,966
I took some fresh air.

69
00:11:08,598 --> 00:11:11,288
Where did you go?

70
00:11:12,487 --> 00:11:14,867
I didn't go far, brother.
I was at Harmankaya.

71
00:11:14,910 --> 00:11:17,540
You are lying to my face!

72
00:11:17,634 --> 00:11:20,984
How can you go to Turgut's tribe
without telling me?

73
00:11:20,997 --> 00:11:24,997
-What are you up to, Mari?
-It's none of your business, brother!

74
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:27,090
Arrogant!

75
00:11:27,194 --> 00:11:31,394
You won't step out of this castle
before marrying Nikola.

76
00:11:31,595 --> 00:11:34,515
Have you heard me?
My eyes are on you!

77
00:11:34,775 --> 00:11:38,045
This marriage will happen tomorrow!

78
00:11:46,694 --> 00:11:48,784
My lady!

79
00:11:49,496 --> 00:11:51,456
My lady, are you alright?

80
00:11:52,554 --> 00:11:56,554
My brother thinks that he can use
me as a pawn. But he is wrong!

81
00:12:03,849 --> 00:12:06,959
I want you to do something
for me, Cornelia.

82
00:12:07,705 --> 00:12:11,705
-This is important for me.
-There is nothing I won't do for you.

83
00:12:12,382 --> 00:12:15,432
Go to Turgut and ask for his help.

84
00:12:17,596 --> 00:12:20,466
He should kidnap me before
marrying Nikola.

85
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:24,703
Do you trust him that much?

86
00:12:24,999 --> 00:12:27,949
I trust him more than anyone right now.

87
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:43,810
The mine is right here, my bey.

88
00:12:49,692 --> 00:12:52,462
The mine is close to the castle.

89
00:12:57,138 --> 00:13:00,018
Whateve happens...

90
00:13:02,047 --> 00:13:04,467
we'll take that mine.

91
00:13:05,241 --> 00:13:07,341
Tell me, Master Davud.

92
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:18,510
The seam of the mine is
efficient.

93
00:13:24,747 --> 00:13:30,377
This means a lots of weapons
for our alps!

94
00:13:32,748 --> 00:13:35,498
If we take that mine, my bey...

95
00:13:35,685 --> 00:13:40,195
I can make the sharpest
arrowheads.

96
00:13:40,605 --> 00:13:44,325
I can make the strongest balls
that will pierce the walls.

97
00:13:44,547 --> 00:13:48,547
Everything that we need
is in this mine.

98
00:13:49,017 --> 00:13:51,147
The mine is so fertile that...

99
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:54,790
we can even trade with the
weapons I will forge.

100
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:58,320
Mashallah, Master Davud.

101
00:13:59,009 --> 00:14:01,799
We didn't send the master there
for nothing.

102
00:14:03,697 --> 00:14:07,697
The iron that meets your forge
will surely become a weapon.

103
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:15,390
But it's difficult, my bey.
We need to pass the İnegöl borders.

104
00:14:23,018 --> 00:14:26,288
May God forgive Priest Gregor's
sins.

105
00:14:26,717 --> 00:14:30,047
He had only one job!
Only one job!

106
00:14:30,289 --> 00:14:33,309
Placing the flying fire!
He couldn't even do that!

107
00:14:33,452 --> 00:14:36,562
His God can forgive him if
he wants, I won't!

108
00:14:36,595 --> 00:14:40,595
Priest Gregor was my friend! Watch your
words when you speak his name!

109
00:14:41,098 --> 00:14:45,018
-He died fighting for our cause!
-What happened has happened.

110
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:48,590
You won't fight for a dead priest,
will you?

111
00:14:53,653 --> 00:14:56,363
İznik's governor, Saguros.

112
00:15:06,506 --> 00:15:09,136
Governor Saguros.

113
00:15:17,539 --> 00:15:20,019
What a pleasent surprise.

114
00:15:20,098 --> 00:15:21,778
We didn't expect you.

115
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:26,579
I didn't come here for a visit,
but to warn you.

116
00:15:28,927 --> 00:15:31,387
-About what?
-About what?

117
00:15:31,791 --> 00:15:35,561
About the attack on Osman Bey
on the Nikea Road!

118
00:15:40,139 --> 00:15:43,379
Osman is our enemy.

119
00:15:44,822 --> 00:15:46,742
Don't be arrogant, Kosses!

120
00:15:50,759 --> 00:15:53,989
They tried to poison him in my castle!

121
00:15:55,132 --> 00:16:00,582
The attackers on the road keep
attacking in my palace.

122
00:16:11,614 --> 00:16:15,614
I attacked Osman!

123
00:16:19,587 --> 00:16:22,337
I would do it again!

124
00:16:23,067 --> 00:16:26,117
You are the one who trades with Osman...

125
00:16:26,222 --> 00:16:29,462
faces us and shadows the cross!

126
00:16:33,811 --> 00:16:36,681
After all, me and my friends...

127
00:16:43,704 --> 00:16:48,354
we know not to trust
the Turks.

128
00:16:53,123 --> 00:16:55,463
What about you, Saguros?

129
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:59,490
How do you know that Osman
didn't poison you?

130
00:17:01,748 --> 00:17:06,218
Look, he became a hero
in your eyes...

131
00:17:06,421 --> 00:17:09,701
and a friend at your side.

132
00:17:10,656 --> 00:17:14,047
You are a babbler, Nikola.

133
00:17:14,885 --> 00:17:20,155
The tongue might be the end of
many powerful people.

134
00:17:23,771 --> 00:17:25,982
Saguros...

135
00:17:26,601 --> 00:17:29,421
even the strongest men...

136
00:17:29,588 --> 00:17:32,828
get vanished in these times...

137
00:17:34,047 --> 00:17:36,577
like little flies...

138
00:17:37,419 --> 00:17:40,379
and I'm not the one
talking carelessly.

139
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,660
It's you.

140
00:17:42,922 --> 00:17:46,922
And also, it's you who
united with Osman...

141
00:17:48,291 --> 00:17:51,001
and betrayed us.

142
00:18:03,159 --> 00:18:04,999
Lords!

143
00:18:05,388 --> 00:18:08,218
I'm Saguros...

144
00:18:08,396 --> 00:18:10,896
the governor of Nikea!

145
00:18:13,502 --> 00:18:17,192
I'm going to visit Kayı Tribe.

146
00:18:19,042 --> 00:18:22,872
Osman Bey will protect my
caravans...

147
00:18:23,110 --> 00:18:25,620
and my goods.

148
00:18:26,968 --> 00:18:30,768
And you will accept it...

149
00:18:31,158 --> 00:18:35,158
either easily or hardly.

150
00:18:37,988 --> 00:18:41,308
This is my last word.

151
00:18:49,105 --> 00:18:51,435
Every throne is slippery...

152
00:18:52,481 --> 00:18:55,641
in these lands, Saguros.

153
00:18:56,067 --> 00:18:57,897
Be careful.

154
00:18:58,479 --> 00:19:00,599
Farewell.

155
00:19:34,201 --> 00:19:36,181
What do you think, my bey?

156
00:19:36,679 --> 00:19:39,299
How will we pass the İnegöl border?

157
00:19:42,165 --> 00:19:45,465
There is a solution for every trouble.

158
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:49,480
I didn't invite Governor Saguros
for nothing, Master Davud.

159
00:19:50,016 --> 00:19:52,426
We'll enter İnegöl
with his caravan.

160
00:19:52,781 --> 00:19:55,471
The mine isn't just for weapons.

161
00:19:57,076 --> 00:20:02,316
For the conquest of the İnegöl,
we must surround it first.

162
00:20:06,012 --> 00:20:08,762
We'll work on it piece by piece.

163
00:20:11,148 --> 00:20:15,358
When the time comes,
they all will appear.

164
00:20:17,255 --> 00:20:21,935
Having Saguros on our side will
make the lords divide.

165
00:20:24,883 --> 00:20:25,883
This...

166
00:20:29,024 --> 00:20:30,964
will benefit us.

167
00:20:38,763 --> 00:20:40,223
May I enter...

168
00:20:40,628 --> 00:20:43,188
Aygül Hatun?

169
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:50,630
Look, I'm coming in?

170
00:21:00,290 --> 00:21:02,450
Mad girl?

171
00:21:03,827 --> 00:21:05,597
Where are you?

172
00:21:08,868 --> 00:21:09,938
No?

173
00:21:11,099 --> 00:21:13,359
Where are you mad girl?

174
00:22:29,589 --> 00:22:33,149
-What's wrong with your face?
-I'm coming from a mission.

175
00:22:41,519 --> 00:22:45,519
Did you forget your tent?
What are you doing here?

176
00:22:46,223 --> 00:22:47,993
I'm looking for you.

177
00:22:49,847 --> 00:22:55,087
I'll return to my mission in the morning.
I wanted to see you.

178
00:22:57,446 --> 00:22:59,776
I came to see you.

179
00:23:14,602 --> 00:23:18,602
In mine, when I was
working in the darkness...

180
00:23:20,131 --> 00:23:22,591
I saw this stone.

181
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:26,350
It glowed in the darkness.

182
00:23:29,145 --> 00:23:31,845
It reminded me of you.

183
00:23:34,363 --> 00:23:36,413
You enlighten my darkness...

184
00:23:36,821 --> 00:23:39,281
just like this stone.

185
00:23:43,742 --> 00:23:45,752
Cerkutay.

186
00:23:51,979 --> 00:23:53,859
Say yes, girl!

187
00:23:54,232 --> 00:23:55,912
Isn't it enough waiting?

188
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:58,129
-Move, Cerkutay!
-Say yes to me!

189
00:23:58,207 --> 00:24:00,477
-No, I won't
-You won't?

190
00:24:00,531 --> 00:24:03,791
-Come on!
-I hope the mine falls on my head!

191
00:24:03,901 --> 00:24:06,121
And you will feel guilty.

192
00:24:06,141 --> 00:24:09,991
-You will wish you said yes.
-I won't, Cerkutay. I won't.

193
00:24:10,107 --> 00:24:13,727
You soiled everywhere!
Move!

194
00:24:13,777 --> 00:24:16,247
-You will regret it?
-I won't!

195
00:24:16,260 --> 00:24:20,420
I'm going!
I'm gone!

196
00:24:31,209 --> 00:24:32,649
Crazy.

197
00:24:34,401 --> 00:24:36,521
Crazy man.

198
00:24:46,409 --> 00:24:49,469
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come.

199
00:24:59,814 --> 00:25:03,814
What's wrong, Cornelia?
What are you doing here?

200
00:25:05,917 --> 00:25:10,107
-Nothing bad happened, right?
-Turgut Bey. I brought news from Mari.

201
00:25:13,625 --> 00:25:15,365
I'm listening.

202
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:23,153
Lord Kosses.

203
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:26,760
He wants to force her to marry Nikola.

204
00:25:27,217 --> 00:25:29,387
Nikola.

205
00:25:30,549 --> 00:25:33,529
-When is this wedding?
-Tomorrow.

206
00:25:33,790 --> 00:25:35,880
Tomorrow?

207
00:25:36,091 --> 00:25:39,311
What's this hurry?
Are they running away from a fire?

208
00:25:39,755 --> 00:25:42,165
I don't know, sir.

209
00:25:43,486 --> 00:25:45,776
What does she want from me?

210
00:25:46,008 --> 00:25:48,438
To save her.

211
00:25:50,348 --> 00:25:52,768
No one else can help her.

212
00:25:59,853 --> 00:26:02,243
Will you save her?

213
00:26:02,961 --> 00:26:06,961
Firstly, I want to know something.

214
00:26:09,304 --> 00:26:13,304
Your lady, Mari, why does she
trust me?

215
00:26:15,019 --> 00:26:18,599
You can ask her personally
when you save her.

216
00:26:20,236 --> 00:26:24,216
Good. Go, then. I'll give my answer.

217
00:26:25,778 --> 00:26:27,858
Alright, sir.
If you allow me.

218
00:26:27,934 --> 00:26:31,934
Serhan, accompany Cornelia
on the way.

219
00:26:41,390 --> 00:26:43,500
Look at this nomad Osman!

220
00:26:43,556 --> 00:26:49,216
He swayed Governor Saguros to his
side. He wants to break our unity!

221
00:26:51,097 --> 00:26:55,867
We are closer than ever.
We know what to do.

222
00:26:56,846 --> 00:26:59,616
We can't let him hurt us.

223
00:27:00,059 --> 00:27:04,059
Saguros will die like a fly!

224
00:27:04,738 --> 00:27:06,908
If that Saguros...

225
00:27:07,008 --> 00:27:09,788
dies as Osman's guest...

226
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:14,520
the Emperor will send a great
army after Osman.

227
00:27:15,996 --> 00:27:18,106
Only the Emperor?

228
00:27:18,467 --> 00:27:22,037
When Osman went to collide
with Nikea...

229
00:27:24,770 --> 00:27:27,620
I talked to Seljuk vizier Alemşah.

230
00:27:29,631 --> 00:27:32,631
He doesn't like Osman's growth.

231
00:27:34,136 --> 00:27:39,146
Alemşah will go after Osman who's
acting on his own.

232
00:27:39,605 --> 00:27:43,745
Then, we should do our
part too.

233
00:27:45,704 --> 00:27:48,634
Julia, this is a job for
your men.

234
00:27:49,052 --> 00:27:50,822
As you order, lord Lagotus.

235
00:27:51,636 --> 00:27:53,136
Julia.

236
00:27:53,819 --> 00:27:55,979
You'll bring your men to me.

237
00:27:57,644 --> 00:27:59,804
Not only Saguros...

238
00:28:00,327 --> 00:28:01,987
his daughter will die too.

239
00:28:02,774 --> 00:28:05,084
I want a great tragedy.

240
00:28:18,959 --> 00:28:20,199
Alps!

241
00:28:20,283 --> 00:28:21,653
Attention!

242
00:28:46,742 --> 00:28:48,312
Welcome.

243
00:28:48,524 --> 00:28:49,974
Thank you.

244
00:30:17,863 --> 00:30:21,023
Welcome.
Welcome!

245
00:30:21,968 --> 00:30:23,458
Thank you.

246
00:30:23,769 --> 00:30:25,299
Come.

247
00:30:31,286 --> 00:30:32,986
Alps!

248
00:30:34,225 --> 00:30:35,645
Come on!

249
00:32:01,502 --> 00:32:03,322
Mashallah!

250
00:32:06,242 --> 00:32:07,772
Mashallah!

251
00:32:10,489 --> 00:32:14,496
To be honest, I didn't expect
such a mighty greeting.

252
00:32:14,496 --> 00:32:16,796
Respect to the guest...

253
00:32:17,401 --> 00:32:19,251
comes from the glory
of the beylig.

254
00:32:20,356 --> 00:32:21,966
You didn't see anything yet.

255
00:32:22,351 --> 00:32:25,331
Watch the archery drill of the alps.

256
00:32:27,613 --> 00:32:29,283
Alps!

257
00:32:36,409 --> 00:32:37,579
Arrows!

258
00:32:37,871 --> 00:32:38,781
Get ready!

259
00:32:42,367 --> 00:32:43,937
Release!

260
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:54,522
Get ready!

261
00:32:55,652 --> 00:32:56,732
Release!

262
00:33:21,458 --> 00:33:22,778
Turks!

263
00:33:23,044 --> 00:33:25,684
None can beat you at archery.

264
00:33:26,021 --> 00:33:27,721
It's just what we heard.

265
00:33:29,158 --> 00:33:31,168
Even more.

266
00:33:50,018 --> 00:33:51,728
My daughter Hera.

267
00:33:53,008 --> 00:33:55,938
She wanted to meet you and see
your tribe.

268
00:33:57,371 --> 00:33:59,771
-Welcome.
-Thank you.

269
00:33:59,771 --> 00:34:03,311
We couldn't see you at İznik, Hera.
You did well by coming.

270
00:34:03,896 --> 00:34:06,186
I was in Constantinople then.

271
00:34:06,186 --> 00:34:08,786
I'm glad to meet you even if
it's late.

272
00:34:10,574 --> 00:34:14,694
My daughter, if you are curious about
our tribe...

273
00:34:14,694 --> 00:34:17,924
let us show you around.
What do you say?

274
00:34:19,255 --> 00:34:20,696
I would like that.

275
00:34:23,199 --> 00:34:25,099
Then, let's get to the tent.

276
00:34:25,866 --> 00:34:27,759
Let us pass the time of the day.

277
00:34:27,759 --> 00:34:29,536
Gladly, Osman Bey.

278
00:34:29,536 --> 00:34:31,306
Come.

279
00:34:33,710 --> 00:34:35,520
Alright then, come.

280
00:34:50,724 --> 00:34:53,714
Turgut Bey' Tribe

281
00:34:53,746 --> 00:34:55,637
We'll help Mari.

282
00:34:56,553 --> 00:34:58,293
But we can't enter the castle.

283
00:34:59,099 --> 00:35:00,899
We'll kidnap her on the way.

284
00:35:01,063 --> 00:35:03,683
My bey, you say well but...

285
00:35:03,746 --> 00:35:04,866
what if it's a trap?

286
00:35:04,950 --> 00:35:07,220
Mari trusted me and asked
for help.

287
00:35:07,246 --> 00:35:10,946
It doesn't fit us to not hold
the hand that asks for help.

288
00:35:13,261 --> 00:35:15,861
Take your cautions and
ready the alps.

289
00:35:15,914 --> 00:35:18,124
And inform Cornelia personally.

290
00:35:20,330 --> 00:35:22,050
Tomorrow, on the İnegöl road...

291
00:35:23,202 --> 00:35:24,812
we'll kidnap Mari.

292
00:35:27,149 --> 00:35:28,939
As you order, my bey.

293
00:35:45,693 --> 00:35:47,333
For you.

294
00:35:49,610 --> 00:35:52,380
I thought it would fit a bey like you.

295
00:36:03,427 --> 00:36:04,887
Thank you, Mari.

296
00:36:24,224 --> 00:36:27,314
What do you think about the Latins
invading Constantinople?

297
00:36:33,074 --> 00:36:37,404
Years passed after the destruction
of the Catholic Latins.

298
00:36:38,161 --> 00:36:41,751
But the signs of it can still be seen In
Constantinople.

299
00:36:42,220 --> 00:36:44,190
What can I think about it?

300
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:49,620
But everything is well in Constantinople.

301
00:36:50,918 --> 00:36:54,748
With overseas trade and
goods coming from the west...

302
00:36:54,810 --> 00:36:56,730
they live in prosperity.

303
00:36:57,829 --> 00:36:59,169
But...

304
00:36:59,722 --> 00:37:03,482
I hear that some people in Constantinople
want to unite with the Catholics.

305
00:37:05,206 --> 00:37:06,926
Is it wrong?

306
00:37:07,919 --> 00:37:10,839
Fools who lost their memory
can think that.

307
00:37:13,347 --> 00:37:15,737
But that's not what the
majority thinks, Osman Bey.

308
00:37:17,728 --> 00:37:21,938
So, they should've realized that...

309
00:37:21,981 --> 00:37:25,361
the crusades hurt them
before anyone else.

310
00:37:29,777 --> 00:37:32,647
How are things in Seljuks?

311
00:37:32,860 --> 00:37:37,110
We hear that they are oppressed by
the Mongols in Konya.

312
00:37:44,393 --> 00:37:46,133
They reign.

313
00:37:47,969 --> 00:37:51,459
When is it ever seen that those
who stand up against Turks lived forever?

314
00:37:54,199 --> 00:37:56,689
They won't live long either.

315
00:37:59,262 --> 00:38:02,812
Sultan Mesut's resistance is
important for us too.

316
00:38:03,099 --> 00:38:06,089
He is a wall between us and the Mongols.

317
00:38:08,653 --> 00:38:11,403
May God be with them
against the Mongols.

318
00:38:13,326 --> 00:38:14,896
Thank you.

319
00:38:16,298 --> 00:38:18,538
Allah is with those who
have faith.

320
00:38:19,937 --> 00:38:24,527
Surely, the enemies have
a common end.

321
00:38:40,837 --> 00:38:42,577
Ya hak!

322
00:38:46,635 --> 00:38:47,975
Boran.

323
00:39:17,035 --> 00:39:18,205
Swing it!

324
00:39:35,446 --> 00:39:36,836
Alps!

325
00:39:37,877 --> 00:39:39,877
This is easy for Göktuğ.

326
00:39:40,782 --> 00:39:42,992
Swing it harder.

327
00:39:44,708 --> 00:39:46,208
Swing it!

328
00:39:57,550 --> 00:40:00,040
Can you shoot this well?

329
00:40:02,978 --> 00:40:05,798
Come on, girls!
Show her.

330
00:40:06,109 --> 00:40:07,479
Come on.

331
00:40:48,107 --> 00:40:49,607
Mashallah.

332
00:40:59,280 --> 00:41:00,840
Ya hak!
Ya hak!

333
00:41:02,009 --> 00:41:04,329
Mashallah to my daughters.

334
00:41:09,064 --> 00:41:10,204
Amazing.

335
00:41:12,901 --> 00:41:14,361
Swing it!

336
00:41:31,281 --> 00:41:33,401
We'll eat dinner at Söğüt.

337
00:41:33,627 --> 00:41:36,237
Before it we can see...

338
00:41:36,553 --> 00:41:38,853
the goods and manufactories
that brought you here.

339
00:41:39,090 --> 00:41:41,150
I really want to see that.

340
00:41:41,293 --> 00:41:44,293
I'm so happy to trade with you, Osman Bey.

341
00:41:46,206 --> 00:41:50,216
This trade will strengthen you and
Nikea.

342
00:41:51,459 --> 00:41:53,179
Inshallah.

343
00:42:10,198 --> 00:42:11,638
How can that happen?

344
00:42:12,104 --> 00:42:13,944
Do you have a secret?

345
00:42:14,790 --> 00:42:16,790
The secret is here, my girl.

346
00:42:18,633 --> 00:42:21,293
But we have another secret.

347
00:42:21,823 --> 00:42:23,812
We are nomads.

348
00:42:23,812 --> 00:42:28,682
And while moving we always
look for trouble.

349
00:42:30,063 --> 00:42:33,883
So, we train our children
when they are little.

350
00:42:35,366 --> 00:42:37,686
Without discriminating by gender.

351
00:42:39,215 --> 00:42:42,535
Now let's see how you do it.

352
00:42:43,422 --> 00:42:45,032
Come on.

353
00:42:45,527 --> 00:42:47,157
Come on, try it.

354
00:43:05,132 --> 00:43:07,032
I knew that would happen.

355
00:43:07,407 --> 00:43:09,787
I can't do it.
I'm not as good as you.

356
00:43:13,347 --> 00:43:14,777
Göktuğ!

357
00:43:18,565 --> 00:43:20,105
Come here.

358
00:43:20,950 --> 00:43:22,600
-Yes, mother.
-Come.

359
00:43:30,780 --> 00:43:33,350
Look, my daughter.
This is Göktuğ.

360
00:43:34,008 --> 00:43:35,868
He is a talented archer.

361
00:43:36,046 --> 00:43:38,426
He can teach you how to
shoot arrows.

362
00:43:39,768 --> 00:43:42,338
Not at all, mother.
I can share what I know.

363
00:43:42,939 --> 00:43:45,779
You are, son.
You are a good archer.

364
00:43:46,960 --> 00:43:49,230
Talent deserves admiration.

365
00:43:49,358 --> 00:43:51,868
Teach her well how to do it.

366
00:43:52,091 --> 00:43:55,331
When your drill ends, you can
bring our guest back.

367
00:43:58,832 --> 00:44:00,132
Alright, mother.

368
00:44:14,234 --> 00:44:17,414
Ladies, would you like to drink
something?

369
00:44:19,691 --> 00:44:22,911
Come on, there are things to
do in the tent.

370
00:44:23,007 --> 00:44:25,137
Come on. To our jobs!

371
00:44:34,543 --> 00:44:36,473
The girl is pretty.

372
00:44:36,713 --> 00:44:38,343
And single.

373
00:44:39,191 --> 00:44:43,171
Listen to your mother Selcan and
don't miss that.

374
00:44:44,572 --> 00:44:46,072
Mother.

375
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:53,724
Don't blush, son.
Don't blush.

376
00:44:53,724 --> 00:44:56,012
They are your sisters,
not strangers.

377
00:44:56,012 --> 00:44:57,512
Go on.

378
00:45:06,034 --> 00:45:08,394
You don't miss anything, mother.

379
00:45:09,092 --> 00:45:11,292
Looking is for the eyes, my daughter.

380
00:45:11,387 --> 00:45:13,087
Seeing is for the heart.

381
00:45:25,417 --> 00:45:28,227
Firstly, we'll wear this ring.

382
00:45:43,076 --> 00:45:44,726
Come.

383
00:46:02,889 --> 00:46:04,679
You'll stand like this.

384
00:46:05,537 --> 00:46:07,557
Take your arrow...

385
00:46:12,029 --> 00:46:13,909
look at your target...

386
00:46:17,739 --> 00:46:19,619
draw your bow...

387
00:46:27,269 --> 00:46:28,799
Amazing!

388
00:46:31,175 --> 00:46:33,165
Will I be able to shoot this good?

389
00:46:33,563 --> 00:46:37,433
Of course, if you train well,
you will be a good archer.

390
00:46:41,407 --> 00:46:43,127
Come on, try it.

391
00:46:59,037 --> 00:47:00,207
Draw it.

392
00:47:01,672 --> 00:47:03,472
Hold it a little above.

393
00:47:04,103 --> 00:47:06,593
Look at your target,
draw your bow.

394
00:47:15,658 --> 00:47:17,158
Just like this.

395
00:47:25,729 --> 00:47:29,119
Saguros and his daughter will die.

396
00:47:29,864 --> 00:47:31,394
I don't want any mistake.

397
00:47:31,426 --> 00:47:33,706
You'll do what's needed.

398
00:47:39,217 --> 00:47:41,097
Governor Saguros...

399
00:47:41,308 --> 00:47:44,498
and his daughter won't leave
Söğüt alive.

400
00:47:49,855 --> 00:47:51,885
And the responsible...

401
00:47:54,729 --> 00:47:56,849
will be Osman.

402
00:48:10,296 --> 00:48:11,876
May I enter, mother.

403
00:48:12,814 --> 00:48:14,474
Come, son.

404
00:48:16,757 --> 00:48:17,907
You summoned me.

405
00:48:18,822 --> 00:48:20,902
Come, come.
Sit here.

406
00:48:29,599 --> 00:48:32,709
Tell me.

407
00:48:33,199 --> 00:48:35,929
How was it?
Did you teach her well?

408
00:48:38,153 --> 00:48:39,963
Was she a good teacher?

409
00:48:40,937 --> 00:48:41,977
She learned, mother.

410
00:48:42,868 --> 00:48:45,178
She learned.
She is talented.

411
00:48:45,184 --> 00:48:48,594
You wouldn't call her a Rum girl.

412
00:48:50,488 --> 00:48:52,538
It's apparent.
She is talented.

413
00:48:53,354 --> 00:48:55,384
She shot the target.

414
00:48:57,199 --> 00:48:59,429
Wait, mother.
Don't make me shy.

415
00:48:59,977 --> 00:49:02,367
There is no shyness in love, son.

416
00:49:04,781 --> 00:49:08,871
You open your chest against
spears and swords...

417
00:49:08,876 --> 00:49:11,306
are you afraid of love?

418
00:49:13,144 --> 00:49:15,634
There are possible things and
impossible things, mother.

419
00:49:15,905 --> 00:49:17,595
She is the governor's daughter.

420
00:49:18,976 --> 00:49:21,736
I'm an alps with nothing else
but his sword.

421
00:49:23,555 --> 00:49:25,265
How can I compete.

422
00:49:27,234 --> 00:49:30,124
If I dream for impossible,
I can't be happy.

423
00:49:30,576 --> 00:49:32,456
What is impossible?

424
00:49:32,805 --> 00:49:34,605
You have a heart.

425
00:49:36,038 --> 00:49:40,198
Don't we all pray to Allah
who is all capable, Göktuğ?

426
00:49:40,428 --> 00:49:41,618
Huh?

427
00:49:42,853 --> 00:49:45,633
Only he holds the hearts.

428
00:49:45,824 --> 00:49:48,694
If he wrote it, no one can
erase it.

429
00:49:51,577 --> 00:49:53,525
And if she is the governor's daughter...

430
00:49:53,525 --> 00:49:57,245
you are Osman Bey's
lion alp.

431
00:49:57,439 --> 00:49:58,549
Huh?

432
00:49:59,770 --> 00:50:03,410
If the love is in your heart,
you won't give up.

433
00:50:05,054 --> 00:50:08,545
I will tell your Osman Bey.
We'll go and ask for Hera.

434
00:50:08,545 --> 00:50:09,935
Alright, my lion?

435
00:50:10,845 --> 00:50:12,315
Really, mother?

436
00:50:13,444 --> 00:50:15,354
Do you think the governor will
accept it?

437
00:50:15,953 --> 00:50:18,903
Wouldn't he? After Osman Bey asks?

438
00:50:19,386 --> 00:50:22,616
But, you should make
sure of the girl's heart first.

439
00:50:31,713 --> 00:50:33,113
Thank you, mother.

440
00:50:33,634 --> 00:50:35,604
-Thank you.
-You too, son.

441
00:50:35,635 --> 00:50:37,055
You too.

442
00:50:40,736 --> 00:50:42,636
Harmankaya Castle

443
00:50:52,041 --> 00:50:54,321
-Stop, what are you doing?
-It's me, Serhan.

444
00:50:54,999 --> 00:50:57,169
We'll kidnap Mari on
the İnegöl Road.

445
00:50:58,494 --> 00:51:00,374
Thank God.

446
00:51:00,992 --> 00:51:03,385
My lady will be so happy.

447
00:51:03,385 --> 00:51:05,105
I'm grateful.

448
00:51:09,514 --> 00:51:11,924
Söğüt

449
00:51:12,367 --> 00:51:15,317
Welcome, my bey!
Welcome, my bey!

450
00:51:21,380 --> 00:51:23,200
Thank you!

451
00:51:28,385 --> 00:51:30,725
Thank you!
Thank you!

452
00:51:50,899 --> 00:51:52,249
Thank you!

453
00:51:52,742 --> 00:51:54,002
Thank you!

454
00:51:54,326 --> 00:51:56,126
Good day!

455
00:52:02,717 --> 00:52:04,297
Good day!

456
00:52:19,374 --> 00:52:21,194
May your business prosper.

457
00:52:21,194 --> 00:52:22,434
Good day!

458
00:52:22,854 --> 00:52:25,003
Allah bless you, my bey.

459
00:52:25,003 --> 00:52:28,613
I didn't know that you Turks
urbanized like this.

460
00:52:29,219 --> 00:52:31,009
You must've put in some real effort.

461
00:52:31,602 --> 00:52:33,902
We'll urbanize even more, inshallah.

462
00:52:34,917 --> 00:52:37,677
It's all for the prosperity
of the people.

463
00:52:44,255 --> 00:52:46,197
Welcome, Selcan Hatun!

464
00:52:46,197 --> 00:52:47,931
Salam Alaikum.

465
00:52:47,931 --> 00:52:50,381
-Good day.
-Welcome, my lady.

466
00:52:50,574 --> 00:52:51,704
Look.

467
00:52:55,156 --> 00:52:57,386
You will like Söğüt.

468
00:52:58,152 --> 00:52:59,632
It seems like.

469
00:53:04,866 --> 00:53:08,236
It's the craft of our women. They
make it from madder.

470
00:53:08,499 --> 00:53:09,809
Is that so?

471
00:53:13,335 --> 00:53:14,885
It's really pretty.

472
00:53:15,184 --> 00:53:17,154
Let it be a memento.

473
00:53:17,858 --> 00:53:20,358
I'm grateful, Bala Hatun.
Thank you.

474
00:53:20,461 --> 00:53:22,041
I'll always keep it.

475
00:53:27,520 --> 00:53:29,480
Thank you.

476
00:53:31,504 --> 00:53:33,074
Come on.

477
00:53:34,739 --> 00:53:36,499
May Allah prosper you.

478
00:53:43,763 --> 00:53:45,663
Come, my girl.
Come.

479
00:53:53,854 --> 00:53:56,094
-Welcome, Osman Bey!
-Thank you.

480
00:53:57,833 --> 00:53:59,443
Thank you.

481
00:54:00,194 --> 00:54:01,594
Thank you.

482
00:54:21,535 --> 00:54:22,955
My sheik!

483
00:54:25,926 --> 00:54:27,566
My sheik Edebali!

484
00:54:28,741 --> 00:54:32,371
-Governor Saguros.
-Welcome, Governor Saguros.

485
00:54:32,678 --> 00:54:34,268
Thank you.

486
00:54:43,276 --> 00:54:44,676
Wait.

487
00:54:44,952 --> 00:54:46,182
Not now.

488
00:54:46,506 --> 00:54:47,996
Wait for him to separate
from Osman.

489
00:54:53,871 --> 00:54:55,811
Our target is Saguros.

490
00:55:05,867 --> 00:55:07,617
Salam Alaikum.

491
00:55:07,862 --> 00:55:09,112
And Alaikum Salam.

492
00:55:09,588 --> 00:55:11,538
Alaikum Salam.

493
00:55:12,989 --> 00:55:14,799
Yes, Turgut Bey.

494
00:55:15,220 --> 00:55:18,100
There is something important, Osman Bey.

495
00:55:19,323 --> 00:55:21,623
Of course, if you have time.

496
00:55:27,340 --> 00:55:29,150
Then, let's speak at the inn.

497
00:55:54,762 --> 00:55:56,517
Did you sleep well, Nikola?

498
00:55:56,517 --> 00:55:58,047
No.

499
00:55:58,276 --> 00:55:59,796
Not at all.

500
00:56:00,716 --> 00:56:03,396
I thought about Saguros until
morning.

501
00:56:04,166 --> 00:56:08,236
I thought about what will happen
to Osman when he dies.

502
00:56:09,337 --> 00:56:10,997
Don't worry, Nikola.

503
00:56:11,112 --> 00:56:14,072
Our plan will succeed this time.

504
00:56:14,113 --> 00:56:15,723
Don't worry.

505
00:56:17,285 --> 00:56:20,385
Do you know why else I couldn't
sleep?

506
00:56:22,986 --> 00:56:24,746
Mari.

507
00:56:31,641 --> 00:56:34,551
You still haven't told me anything.

508
00:56:37,059 --> 00:56:39,049
Have you talked to Mari, Kosses.

509
00:56:41,923 --> 00:56:47,363
I'm afraid, you'll have to convince
her personally, Nikola.

510
00:56:56,011 --> 00:56:57,531
You are right.

511
00:56:58,071 --> 00:57:00,801
When Mari sees how much I value her...

512
00:57:01,205 --> 00:57:03,865
after seeing the gifts I bring her...

513
00:57:04,145 --> 00:57:08,005
without a doubt.

514
00:57:24,097 --> 00:57:25,957
Any good news?

515
00:57:27,954 --> 00:57:30,644
Turgut Bey will save you at the
İnegöl Road.

516
00:58:00,808 --> 00:58:02,668
Dear Mari.

517
00:58:05,577 --> 00:58:07,087
Welcome.

518
00:58:10,697 --> 00:58:12,737
I should leave you alone.

519
00:58:13,332 --> 00:58:16,362
I hope you'll make the right
decision.

520
00:58:29,745 --> 00:58:31,795
I'm sorry, Mari.

521
00:58:33,377 --> 00:58:37,747
I should've come to you first
for such a delicate matter.

522
00:58:41,100 --> 00:58:42,810
Forgive me.

523
00:58:45,879 --> 00:58:48,409
If you say yes to me...

524
00:58:53,067 --> 00:58:56,767
everything I own will be yours.

525
00:59:00,039 --> 00:59:01,679
The greatest...

526
00:59:03,971 --> 00:59:07,041
the greatest gift that I can
give you...

527
00:59:20,835 --> 00:59:22,645
aren't these.

528
00:59:40,334 --> 00:59:41,774
I offer you...

529
00:59:42,666 --> 00:59:45,166
endless happiness.

530
00:59:48,694 --> 00:59:50,664
Mari with pretty eyes.

531
00:59:52,628 --> 00:59:54,518
Will you marry me?

532
01:00:04,206 --> 01:00:06,386
When you marry me...

533
01:00:06,454 --> 01:00:08,954
what will change in your life, Nikola?

534
01:00:10,170 --> 01:00:11,670
Many things.

535
01:00:12,317 --> 01:00:16,177
Our loyalty to each other will
make us much more stronger.

536
01:00:17,759 --> 01:00:19,629
Loyalty and power.

537
01:00:19,677 --> 01:00:21,387
Is it enough for a marriage?

538
01:00:22,881 --> 01:00:24,491
Of course not.

539
01:00:24,883 --> 01:00:27,473
Amor, Mari.
Amor.

540
01:00:27,834 --> 01:00:29,274
Love.

541
01:00:29,492 --> 01:00:31,322
Belive me, Mari.

542
01:00:34,693 --> 01:00:38,193
Even a fire without love
is in darkness.

543
01:00:39,000 --> 01:00:41,730
And I, Aya Nikola,
promise you...

544
01:00:42,348 --> 01:00:46,068
we'll never be in darkness
for a second in our lives.

545
01:00:46,796 --> 01:00:48,386
I promise you.

546
01:00:53,536 --> 01:00:55,136
I hope so, Nikola.

547
01:01:13,487 --> 01:01:16,727
We'll be so strong and
so happy, Mari.

548
01:01:18,315 --> 01:01:20,375
You will never regret it.

549
01:01:20,578 --> 01:01:22,048
Never.

550
01:01:30,182 --> 01:01:32,042
Mari informed me.

551
01:01:32,093 --> 01:01:34,673
I didn't know what to do.
I wanted to ask you.

552
01:01:34,939 --> 01:01:38,299
His brother Kosses. Even though
she doesn't want it...

553
01:01:39,100 --> 01:01:41,400
he is forcing her to
marry Nikola.

554
01:01:42,244 --> 01:01:43,814
What does she want from you?

555
01:01:44,674 --> 01:01:46,384
To save her.

556
01:01:49,050 --> 01:01:50,670
It's the customs of the Turks.

557
01:01:51,307 --> 01:01:54,287
Those who need help get
helped.

558
01:01:56,737 --> 01:01:58,977
I will kidnap Mari, Osman Bey.

559
01:02:00,531 --> 01:02:05,381
But more importantly, what's Nikola's
goal on this marriage?

560
01:02:06,292 --> 01:02:11,312
Nikola wants to marry Mari and strenghten
his ties with Kosses.

561
01:02:12,974 --> 01:02:15,074
But we'll be more nimble.

562
01:02:15,723 --> 01:02:17,973
We'll stop that.

563
01:02:18,818 --> 01:02:22,278
By taking Mari, we'll hurt the lords.

564
01:02:23,566 --> 01:02:27,656
And when Nikola can't find what he
expected, their relation will get hurt.

565
01:02:28,170 --> 01:02:30,290
They'll lose their unity.

566
01:02:31,308 --> 01:02:33,778
Taking Mari will separate them.

567
01:02:36,408 --> 01:02:40,348
This will cause many good things.

568
01:02:41,399 --> 01:02:44,319
I will give you my bravest alps.

569
01:02:47,987 --> 01:02:49,877
Thank you, Osman Bey.

570
01:02:56,337 --> 01:02:59,807
Söğüt artisans are working
to deliver the goods.

571
01:03:00,931 --> 01:03:02,741
Welcome, my sheik.

572
01:03:02,902 --> 01:03:04,852
Thank you, Akça.

573
01:03:05,840 --> 01:03:07,910
Dervish Akça.

574
01:03:10,209 --> 01:03:13,169
He'll prepare the leather you want.

575
01:03:18,795 --> 01:03:20,455
It's high quality.

576
01:03:27,037 --> 01:03:28,287
Interesting.

577
01:03:30,600 --> 01:03:32,360
There is no difference in quality.

578
01:03:32,523 --> 01:03:34,093
How do you assure that?

579
01:03:35,486 --> 01:03:38,986
Don't your masters ever
make bad crafts?

580
01:03:40,789 --> 01:03:44,189
Firstly, the boots you liked...

581
01:03:44,555 --> 01:03:46,975
is a gift from me to you.

582
01:03:50,632 --> 01:03:52,982
And the answer to your question...

583
01:03:53,638 --> 01:03:56,298
this is why we have the Ahi Order.

584
01:03:57,305 --> 01:04:00,795
Firstly, we hire by competence.

585
01:04:01,949 --> 01:04:06,089
Not even a single person who doesn't
deserve it can get the job.

586
01:04:11,225 --> 01:04:13,215
They can't get approval.

587
01:04:13,972 --> 01:04:17,382
All the masters are taught from
apprenticeship.

588
01:04:18,353 --> 01:04:21,913
They are all given jobs according
to their competence.

589
01:04:23,373 --> 01:04:26,393
But, the real thing is...

590
01:04:26,874 --> 01:04:28,394
morals.

591
01:04:31,237 --> 01:04:34,937
Our prophet, Hz.Muhammad...

592
01:04:35,337 --> 01:04:37,567
peace be upon him...

593
01:04:38,233 --> 01:04:40,033
was also a trader.

594
01:04:40,452 --> 01:04:45,042
We follow him in trade,
as in everything else.

595
01:04:45,560 --> 01:04:48,200
We work with his morals.

596
01:04:57,446 --> 01:05:00,036
What are our goals, Akça Dervish?

597
01:05:00,617 --> 01:05:03,077
Making good goods...

598
01:05:03,396 --> 01:05:05,686
and selling them without
getting haram money.

599
01:05:07,086 --> 01:05:10,486
Our only goal is to make
halal money.

600
01:05:10,537 --> 01:05:12,137
Thank you.

601
01:05:17,349 --> 01:05:19,969
That's why, Governor Saguros.

602
01:05:20,665 --> 01:05:24,825
Like all the artisans, Akça makes
the best.

603
01:05:24,978 --> 01:05:27,888
Not at all, my sheik.
We try our best.

604
01:05:30,346 --> 01:05:32,086
Go to the woofer.

605
01:05:32,818 --> 01:05:34,868
If you find one faulty good...

606
01:05:35,211 --> 01:05:37,731
all his goods and money is yours.

607
01:05:39,758 --> 01:05:43,428
Go to the tinner, if you find
one hole...

608
01:05:44,404 --> 01:05:47,044
all his goods are a gift
from me to you.

609
01:06:08,725 --> 01:06:10,405
Governor Saguros!

610
01:06:15,435 --> 01:06:17,775
-My Sheik.
-Governor Saguros...

611
01:06:17,965 --> 01:06:21,205
my bey wanted me to convey it.
Your rooms are ready.

612
01:06:21,249 --> 01:06:23,239
You can rest until dinner.

613
01:06:24,765 --> 01:06:26,575
No need for that.

614
01:06:28,088 --> 01:06:31,028
Your word is the guarantee
of our trade.

615
01:06:31,351 --> 01:06:34,031
-Thank you.
-Now, if you allow me...

616
01:06:34,309 --> 01:06:36,419
I want to take some rest.

617
01:06:36,982 --> 01:06:38,388
Have a nice day.

618
01:06:38,388 --> 01:06:39,448
Come, please.

619
01:06:50,613 --> 01:06:52,243
Damn it!

620
01:07:17,967 --> 01:07:20,537
This thing will be over tonight.

621
01:07:20,537 --> 01:07:22,087
Where are they now?

622
01:07:22,425 --> 01:07:26,255
Osman is hosting a dinner at the inn for
Saguros this evening.

623
01:07:28,154 --> 01:07:30,003
We will sneak into the inn.

624
01:07:30,003 --> 01:07:32,283
We will get the men inside from there.

625
01:07:32,476 --> 01:07:34,796
No one will escape.

626
01:07:34,899 --> 01:07:36,429
What is your plan?

627
01:07:37,692 --> 01:07:39,212
The kitchen.

628
01:07:39,807 --> 01:07:42,907
We will go undercover and get the men
in from there.

629
01:07:43,512 --> 01:07:46,422
Not only Saguros but also his daughter
will die.

630
01:07:47,023 --> 01:07:51,353
This incident must be a big trouble
for Osman.

631
01:08:22,274 --> 01:08:24,044
Good evening.

632
01:08:41,425 --> 01:08:42,694
Here you go.

633
01:08:54,033 --> 01:08:56,734
In the name of Allah, the compassionate,
the merciful.

634
01:09:03,794 --> 01:09:09,254
O our Rabb, who spreads sustenance
to whom he wills without reckoning.

635
01:09:10,171 --> 01:09:13,106
Thank you for your blessings.

636
01:09:13,106 --> 01:09:15,286
-Amen.
-Amen.

637
01:09:16,890 --> 01:09:20,100
O Almighty Rabb...

638
01:09:20,822 --> 01:09:25,352
...grant us the opportunity to taste
these beauties...

639
01:09:25,352 --> 01:09:31,182
...which you made us taste at this table,
in your eternal home, heaven.

640
01:09:32,716 --> 01:09:34,046
Amen.

641
01:09:34,698 --> 01:09:39,468
Grant us to be grateful for
these blessings...

642
01:09:39,468 --> 01:09:43,678
...and to serve you.

643
01:09:44,068 --> 01:09:45,638
Amen.

644
01:10:11,148 --> 01:10:13,748
In the name of Allah, the compassionate,
the merciful.

645
01:10:16,817 --> 01:10:18,417
Here you go.

646
01:10:19,799 --> 01:10:20,952
Here you go.

647
01:10:20,952 --> 01:10:23,872
In the name of Allah, the compassionate,
the merciful.

648
01:10:36,998 --> 01:10:38,838
Come on.

649
01:11:46,473 --> 01:11:49,053
You taught me a lot about archery today.

650
01:11:50,005 --> 01:11:52,365
You are really good at it.

651
01:11:59,147 --> 01:12:01,367
You were no less, Hera.

652
01:12:01,841 --> 01:12:04,661
If you complete your practices
you will become a master too.

653
01:12:35,725 --> 01:12:37,145
No!

654
01:12:45,927 --> 01:12:47,427
Father!

655
01:12:54,391 --> 01:12:56,651
Are you all right?

656
01:12:57,718 --> 01:12:58,778
I am!

657
01:13:00,152 --> 01:13:04,562
On my table, to my guests!
Who did this?

658
01:13:05,340 --> 01:13:07,810
Alps!
Come on!

659
01:13:08,061 --> 01:13:10,841
To the inn, to the Söğüt!
Spread everywhere!

660
01:13:11,526 --> 01:13:13,976
You will find the traitors!

661
01:13:14,227 --> 01:13:15,987
Come on, Alps!

662
01:13:16,110 --> 01:13:18,260
Father! Are you okay, father!

663
01:13:19,123 --> 01:13:21,723
- I am fine.
-You are fine!

664
01:13:24,703 --> 01:13:25,860
Father!

665
01:13:25,860 --> 01:13:28,140
The arrow can be poisonous.

666
01:13:28,617 --> 01:13:31,537
Carry him to the room!
Come on!

667
01:13:32,216 --> 01:13:33,456
-Father! Father!
-Come on!

668
01:13:34,049 --> 01:13:35,729
-Father!
-To the room, come on!

669
01:13:36,704 --> 01:13:38,454
-Göktuğ, Göktuğ!
-Göktuğ

670
01:13:39,825 --> 01:13:41,245
My brother!

671
01:13:50,173 --> 01:13:51,273
Father!

672
01:14:09,048 --> 01:14:10,788
Baysungur!

673
01:14:21,212 --> 01:14:24,172
They just wanted to cook some good
meal for Osman Bey.

674
01:14:25,193 --> 01:14:26,913
But the traitors took their lives.

675
01:14:30,530 --> 01:14:32,020
What is the positon?

676
01:14:40,552 --> 01:14:42,512
They killed them, my Bey.

677
01:14:43,146 --> 01:14:45,566
They wore their clothes.

678
01:14:46,886 --> 01:14:49,382
Find a clue, a trace.

679
01:14:49,382 --> 01:14:51,452
Check everywhere.

680
01:14:52,014 --> 01:14:53,604
Of course, my Bey.

681
01:15:18,591 --> 01:15:19,891
Kumral Abdal.

682
01:15:19,996 --> 01:15:21,836
What is his position, tell us.

683
01:15:22,400 --> 01:15:23,940
I gave him the antidote, my Bey.

684
01:15:25,543 --> 01:15:27,803
But the poison is too strong.

685
01:15:28,811 --> 01:15:31,721
No, no, no!

686
01:15:32,112 --> 01:15:34,272
You are the most skilled healer!

687
01:15:37,653 --> 01:15:39,953
Only you can heal him.

688
01:15:40,811 --> 01:15:43,171
I hope, my Bey. I hope.

689
01:15:57,908 --> 01:15:59,128
O Allah, the healer.

690
01:16:08,401 --> 01:16:10,331
Father!
Father!

691
01:16:12,069 --> 01:16:13,559
Father!

692
01:16:26,987 --> 01:16:28,337
Hera.

693
01:16:29,611 --> 01:16:32,561
Don't upset yourself.
Your father will recover.

694
01:16:54,541 --> 01:16:58,131
I will hang at the door of Söğüt...

695
01:16:58,325 --> 01:17:00,495
...whoever did this...

696
01:17:02,365 --> 01:17:05,075
...at my inn, at my table, at Söğüt.

697
01:17:06,329 --> 01:17:08,669
As soon as I get them.

698
01:17:15,253 --> 01:17:16,793
Kumral Abdal...

699
01:17:17,287 --> 01:17:18,897
...how is Göktuğ?

700
01:17:19,494 --> 01:17:22,834
I gave him the antidote, my Bey.
He is next door.

701
01:17:29,835 --> 01:17:31,530
What happened, Alps?

702
01:17:31,610 --> 01:17:34,140
There was an attack but everyone is fine.
Don't worry.

703
01:17:34,851 --> 01:17:36,951
-Is Osman Bey fine?
- He is.

704
01:17:41,676 --> 01:17:43,176
No need to worry.

705
01:17:47,862 --> 01:17:49,672
What is happening?

706
01:17:50,563 --> 01:17:52,043
What is happening?

707
01:17:55,308 --> 01:17:58,778
Damn it!
Didn't you succeed?

708
01:18:42,521 --> 01:18:43,851
I am grateful to you.

709
01:18:45,174 --> 01:18:48,253
If you weren't there maybe I would
too--

710
01:18:48,253 --> 01:18:50,113
It is nothing.

711
01:18:51,363 --> 01:18:53,573
Protecting you is my duty.

712
01:18:57,428 --> 01:18:58,818
Are you all right?

713
01:19:00,382 --> 01:19:01,552
I am.

714
01:19:34,849 --> 01:19:37,059
Brother, are you all right?

715
01:19:37,981 --> 01:19:39,541
I am fine, brother.

716
01:19:52,665 --> 01:19:54,135
O Allah, the healer.

717
01:20:12,425 --> 01:20:14,705
So your chest is hurting?

718
01:20:16,738 --> 01:20:18,828
It doesn't Kumral Abdal.

719
01:20:19,473 --> 01:20:21,053
It doesn't.

720
01:20:23,650 --> 01:20:25,910
I am not talking about this.

721
01:20:27,613 --> 01:20:29,653
I am talking about this.

722
01:20:29,915 --> 01:20:31,955
Allah, Allah!

723
01:20:32,735 --> 01:20:35,065
The secret is revealed, my Göktuğ!

724
01:20:35,149 --> 01:20:37,289
You solved it!

725
01:20:44,152 --> 01:20:47,132
Look at Osman Bey's valiants!

726
01:20:48,246 --> 01:20:51,046
All of their wounds are bleeding
differently.

727
01:20:52,464 --> 01:20:55,484
Various trials.

728
01:21:11,622 --> 01:21:13,882
Love is a trial.

729
01:21:14,668 --> 01:21:17,368
Sometimes you are trialed by separation...

730
01:21:17,720 --> 01:21:19,740
... sometimes by unity.

731
01:21:23,307 --> 01:21:26,547
Which lover came together with his lover
without a trial?

732
01:21:29,446 --> 01:21:31,456
What if it is impossible?

733
01:21:34,843 --> 01:21:37,283
There is no impossible love.

734
01:21:39,095 --> 01:21:41,352
Listen to what I say.

735
01:21:41,352 --> 01:21:43,392
But not with your ears...

736
01:21:44,633 --> 01:21:47,573
...listen with your hearts, my valiants.

737
01:21:49,785 --> 01:21:52,355
Look how crazy it beats!

738
01:21:54,564 --> 01:21:59,704
In the time of the Prophet, there was
a lover companion named Suheyf.

739
01:22:01,016 --> 01:22:05,766
He neither had a home nor money.

740
01:22:06,663 --> 01:22:11,543
But this is love. It stuck in Suheyf's
heart like an arrow from a bow.

741
01:22:14,063 --> 01:22:17,943
His heart beat saying ''love''.

742
01:22:20,905 --> 01:22:25,315
Suheyf fell in love with the beautiful
Şifa Hatun.

743
01:22:26,040 --> 01:22:29,260
Everybody wanted Şifa Hatun.

744
01:22:29,511 --> 01:22:31,481
But she didn't love any of them.

745
01:22:31,678 --> 01:22:34,188
All she wanted was Allah's blessing.

746
01:22:44,728 --> 01:22:47,138
She asked the Prophet...

747
01:22:47,398 --> 01:22:49,728
...''O Allah's Prophet...

748
01:22:49,971 --> 01:22:53,231
... what should I do to get
Allah's blessing?''

749
01:22:55,163 --> 01:22:58,583
Muhammad, whose name is also beautiful
said...

750
01:22:59,202 --> 01:23:03,842
...''Şifa, the faith of the single man
is half...

751
01:23:05,698 --> 01:23:08,378
...marry so that your faith will be
full.''

752
01:23:10,544 --> 01:23:15,444
And Şifa said ''Then you choose whom
I will marry.''

753
01:23:17,978 --> 01:23:21,268
Our Prophet said...

754
01:23:21,630 --> 01:23:25,910
...I will marry you to the first person
who comes to the morning prayer tomorrow.

755
01:23:28,606 --> 01:23:30,396
She was beautiful.

756
01:23:30,955 --> 01:23:33,285
She had many candidates.

757
01:23:33,397 --> 01:23:36,087
They put golds over her road.

758
01:23:36,225 --> 01:23:40,305
They all slept with the wish of going
first in the morning.

759
01:23:42,726 --> 01:23:44,326
Suheyf...

760
01:23:44,621 --> 01:23:47,401
...didn't see himself as worthy for
Şifa Hatun.

761
01:23:47,655 --> 01:23:50,685
He thought his love was impossible.

762
01:23:51,881 --> 01:23:55,221
His heart beat saying ''Şifa!''.

763
01:23:55,865 --> 01:23:58,505
But he didn't speak.

764
01:23:59,977 --> 01:24:01,927
Didn't he go to the prayer?

765
01:24:02,159 --> 01:24:04,989
He did go...

766
01:24:05,211 --> 01:24:06,921
...but slowly.

767
01:24:10,140 --> 01:24:12,640
Can someone escape his fate?

768
01:24:13,073 --> 01:24:16,323
Could you?

769
01:24:22,017 --> 01:24:24,914
None of the companions were
in love with Şifa Hatun...

770
01:24:24,914 --> 01:24:27,224
...could wake up in the morning.

771
01:24:28,520 --> 01:24:32,800
Despite of his slowness, Suheyf was the
first to enter the mosque.

772
01:24:33,789 --> 01:24:35,859
Did he get his love?

773
01:24:37,264 --> 01:24:39,524
He did!

774
01:24:44,054 --> 01:24:47,004
Is what you see and Allah sees the same,
son?

775
01:24:47,760 --> 01:24:51,390
What he saw as impossible was
his fate.

776
01:24:55,805 --> 01:24:59,265
He walked slowly, took the long road.

777
01:24:59,670 --> 01:25:02,820
But he got his love eventually.

778
01:25:08,783 --> 01:25:10,323
The secret is solved!

779
01:25:10,462 --> 01:25:12,492
did he get his love

780
01:25:13,934 --> 01:25:16,544
Who can stand against love?

781
01:25:17,811 --> 01:25:19,901
No one!

782
01:25:32,572 --> 01:25:34,482
Thank you, Kumral Abdal.

783
01:25:34,762 --> 01:25:36,322
Thank you.

784
01:25:39,539 --> 01:25:40,999
Thank you.

785
01:26:09,015 --> 01:26:11,095
The secret is solved.

786
01:26:11,728 --> 01:26:13,598
The secret is solved.

787
01:26:14,672 --> 01:26:16,392
The secret is solved!

788
01:26:37,138 --> 01:26:38,388
Father!

789
01:26:39,829 --> 01:26:41,269
Father!

790
01:26:42,039 --> 01:26:43,419
Hera.

791
01:26:44,725 --> 01:26:46,145
Hera.

792
01:26:46,764 --> 01:26:48,284
My girl.

793
01:26:48,926 --> 01:26:50,276
Are you all right?

794
01:26:50,689 --> 01:26:51,989
I am.

795
01:26:52,304 --> 01:26:55,534
I am. You are too, Thank God!

796
01:27:00,474 --> 01:27:02,244
Osman Bey.

797
01:27:04,816 --> 01:27:08,516
Did you wait here for me?

798
01:27:13,599 --> 01:27:15,379
I am grateful.

799
01:27:18,016 --> 01:27:19,156
You saved...

800
01:27:20,377 --> 01:27:21,757
...my...

801
01:27:22,495 --> 01:27:25,025
...and my daughter's life.

802
01:27:27,645 --> 01:27:31,035
Who kills and saves is Allah.

803
01:27:33,231 --> 01:27:36,301
The bridge for this healing is
Kumral Abdal.

804
01:27:40,714 --> 01:27:42,124
Anyway.

805
01:27:43,286 --> 01:27:46,016
You rest now.

806
01:27:54,793 --> 01:27:56,333
Father.

807
01:27:57,459 --> 01:27:58,866
My girl.

808
01:27:58,866 --> 01:28:00,916
Thank God you opened your eyes.

809
01:28:39,586 --> 01:28:41,066
Thankfully...

810
01:28:41,505 --> 01:28:43,515
...Saguros is fine.

811
01:28:48,601 --> 01:28:50,081
He is alive.

812
01:28:52,340 --> 01:28:54,940
But we weren't the target.

813
01:28:55,186 --> 01:28:57,206
It was Saguros.

814
01:28:58,499 --> 01:29:02,799
They were going to kill him and then
use that as an excuse to attack us.

815
01:29:04,335 --> 01:29:07,985
Those who can't win in war
play games like this, my Bey.

816
01:29:09,311 --> 01:29:12,001
Thus, we must always be cautious.

817
01:29:13,697 --> 01:29:17,037
Brother, get the Alps ready for war.

818
01:29:19,763 --> 01:29:22,373
We will go to İnegöl with Saguros.

819
01:29:24,728 --> 01:29:29,208
But we will cross the border of İnegöl
with him without using our swords.

820
01:29:30,582 --> 01:29:33,182
Then we will attack the mine.

821
01:29:33,239 --> 01:29:35,099
My Alps are inside.

822
01:29:36,515 --> 01:29:39,055
While they hurt the inside...

823
01:29:39,118 --> 01:29:41,558
...we'll hurt the outside.

824
01:29:41,935 --> 01:29:44,395
Just like a wolfpack.

825
01:29:45,928 --> 01:29:47,678
As you order, my Bey!

826
01:29:58,246 --> 01:30:01,426
Harmankaya Castle

827
01:30:19,479 --> 01:30:20,959
Did you succeed?

828
01:30:23,968 --> 01:30:26,168
The inn got messy, Kosses.

829
01:30:26,523 --> 01:30:28,763
I couldn't even understand what happened.

830
01:30:35,161 --> 01:30:36,991
Go on.

831
01:30:42,149 --> 01:30:44,009
I was waiting outside.

832
01:30:45,387 --> 01:30:48,557
Suddenly, Alps started to move.

833
01:30:48,850 --> 01:30:52,640
I waited but my men didn't come out.

834
01:30:53,725 --> 01:30:55,725
Saguros.

835
01:30:58,856 --> 01:31:02,376
Osman's Alps started searching
all the Söğüt.

836
01:31:05,071 --> 01:31:07,011
I had to run.

837
01:31:08,758 --> 01:31:13,598
There is only one thing I wonder!

838
01:31:14,452 --> 01:31:17,582
Is Saguros dead?

839
01:31:18,294 --> 01:31:20,184
Or not?

840
01:31:22,585 --> 01:31:26,795
Is Saguros dead or not?

841
01:31:27,843 --> 01:31:29,513
He didn't!

842
01:31:35,230 --> 01:31:36,810
Get out!

843
01:31:53,951 --> 01:31:55,441
We came.

844
01:31:55,540 --> 01:31:58,410
You gave us a great greeting and
honored us.

845
01:31:59,072 --> 01:32:02,272
Now you gave the same delicacy for our
leave.

846
01:32:04,582 --> 01:32:07,262
We couldn't let you go alone.

847
01:32:08,328 --> 01:32:09,718
How?

848
01:32:09,862 --> 01:32:13,262
My enemies do their business in secret.

849
01:32:14,134 --> 01:32:17,224
I don't think they would dare to attack
openly.

850
01:32:17,589 --> 01:32:20,149
They don't know where to stop.

851
01:32:20,590 --> 01:32:23,550
But they know how to ambush well.

852
01:32:26,698 --> 01:32:28,418
Don't forget about yesterday.

853
01:32:28,987 --> 01:32:33,177
Thus, me and my Alps will accompany you.

854
01:32:34,774 --> 01:32:37,294
Have you received ambush intelligence?

855
01:32:37,742 --> 01:32:41,672
You're dressed like you're going
to war rather than a road.

856
01:32:44,880 --> 01:32:49,600
Their ambush and their games are like
sand in the desert.

857
01:32:50,619 --> 01:32:55,319
Because we are always on the alert
and always ready for war.

858
01:33:07,167 --> 01:33:09,097
I am grateful to you, Soldier.

859
01:33:09,730 --> 01:33:12,040
You saved my daughter's life.

860
01:33:13,237 --> 01:33:15,807
Thank you. Anyone would do the same.

861
01:33:21,957 --> 01:33:24,647
Your soldiers are like you, Osman Bey.

862
01:33:25,466 --> 01:33:29,936
I am glad I made brave friends like you.

863
01:33:30,501 --> 01:33:32,191
Thank you.

864
01:33:35,375 --> 01:33:38,065
Don't be surprised at their courage.

865
01:33:39,172 --> 01:33:42,482
Since they are not soldiers...

866
01:33:43,111 --> 01:33:44,961
... they are Kayı Alps.

867
01:33:51,737 --> 01:33:53,277
Alps!

868
01:33:53,676 --> 01:33:55,276
Come on!

869
01:34:54,080 --> 01:34:56,280
My beautiful sister.

870
01:35:03,882 --> 01:35:05,972
I hope you will be so happy.

871
01:35:10,861 --> 01:35:12,631
Nikola is a smart man.

872
01:35:13,385 --> 01:35:17,365
I am sure he will make you very happy.

873
01:35:17,700 --> 01:35:19,690
You always thought about me.

874
01:35:19,942 --> 01:35:21,742
You always wanted the best for me.

875
01:35:22,471 --> 01:35:24,271
I am grateful to you, brother.

876
01:35:35,899 --> 01:35:38,719
I haven't seen you this happy for
a long time.

877
01:35:39,580 --> 01:35:42,490
Why not?
Of course, I will be.

878
01:35:42,837 --> 01:35:45,037
This is my sister's happiest day.

879
01:35:48,114 --> 01:35:49,464
Come on.

880
01:35:49,938 --> 01:35:51,428
Soldier!,

881
01:35:52,618 --> 01:35:56,298
I don't want any problem.
Everything will be perfect.

882
01:35:56,737 --> 01:36:00,707
All is as you wish, Sir.
The gifts were safely loaded into the car.

883
01:36:01,866 --> 01:36:03,516
Get ready. We are leaving.

884
01:36:08,108 --> 01:36:10,478
What if Turgut Bey can't make it?

885
01:36:10,747 --> 01:36:12,637
If he can't come.

886
01:36:17,836 --> 01:36:20,066
If I am lucky, Nikola will die...

887
01:36:20,438 --> 01:36:22,768
... and if I am not, don't forget me,
Cornelia.

888
01:38:22,145 --> 01:38:24,445
Sir, someone is coming!

889
01:38:55,634 --> 01:38:57,334
This is Osman!

890
01:39:11,130 --> 01:39:13,910
How dare you pass here, Osman?

891
01:39:15,472 --> 01:39:18,662
We do not answer the dog.
Are we going to answer its tail?

892
01:39:22,902 --> 01:39:24,702
Get out of my way!

893
01:39:32,947 --> 01:39:34,777
Is there a problem?

894
01:39:43,784 --> 01:39:45,604
Is there a problem?

895
01:39:46,244 --> 01:39:48,534
I didn't know you were here, Sir.

896
01:39:48,802 --> 01:39:51,082
Now you do. Open the road!

897
01:40:51,002 --> 01:40:52,802
Inegöl Castle

898
01:41:00,450 --> 01:41:04,510
It is very nice of you to send your tailor
for the wedding suit, Rogatus.

899
01:41:05,104 --> 01:41:06,804
Thank you.

900
01:41:09,679 --> 01:41:11,819
Do you think it will be ready on time?

901
01:41:14,667 --> 01:41:15,907
Hmm?

902
01:41:18,979 --> 01:41:21,299
He is not just the best tailor...

903
01:41:21,310 --> 01:41:24,070
...he is also the fastest, Nikola.

904
01:41:26,269 --> 01:41:28,099
It's done, Sir.

905
01:41:39,075 --> 01:41:41,635
Good. Good.

906
01:41:44,004 --> 01:41:46,084
There is also something bad.

907
01:41:50,007 --> 01:41:52,777
Lord Saguros and his daughter
is still alive.

908
01:41:53,676 --> 01:41:55,016
What?

909
01:41:55,827 --> 01:41:57,397
How?

910
01:41:58,427 --> 01:42:01,907
My men injured Saguros but couldn't
get out alive.

911
01:42:02,657 --> 01:42:05,011
Damn it!
Damn it!

912
01:42:05,011 --> 01:42:07,824
Damn it!
I will kill all of them myself!

913
01:42:07,824 --> 01:42:09,534
Myself!

914
01:42:10,429 --> 01:42:13,519
Since your clumsy men couldn't kill him...

915
01:42:13,556 --> 01:42:16,556
...I'll be wearing battle armor,
not a wedding suit.

916
01:42:19,006 --> 01:42:20,511
Get my armor!

917
01:42:20,511 --> 01:42:23,321
You should've done it then!

918
01:43:00,138 --> 01:43:01,928
They are coming, my Bey.

919
01:43:03,464 --> 01:43:05,264
Let them.

920
01:43:06,906 --> 01:43:08,536
Alps!

921
01:43:09,511 --> 01:43:11,542
You know what to do!

922
01:43:11,542 --> 01:43:13,372
Yes, my Bey!

923
01:43:24,084 --> 01:43:25,724
My dear friend...

924
01:43:26,010 --> 01:43:27,730
... am I stupid?

925
01:43:27,823 --> 01:43:31,325
Would I marry for love like stupid
people?

926
01:43:31,325 --> 01:43:32,805
Am I dumb?

927
01:43:33,265 --> 01:43:35,447
Power, Rogatus!
Power!

928
01:43:35,447 --> 01:43:38,947
More! More! More! More!

929
01:43:39,980 --> 01:43:42,560
We have to be family for that.

930
01:43:42,638 --> 01:43:46,558
Now you seem to have changed your mind.

931
01:43:46,840 --> 01:43:48,320
Never!

932
01:43:48,397 --> 01:43:51,247
No one can stop me from marrying Mari.

933
01:43:52,766 --> 01:43:55,056
You should watch your words.

934
01:44:04,542 --> 01:44:06,032
Rogatus...

935
01:44:06,631 --> 01:44:09,361
...we need to take a break from this
fight.

936
01:44:09,361 --> 01:44:10,501
For now.

937
01:44:32,727 --> 01:44:34,467
Lord Saguros.

938
01:44:34,673 --> 01:44:38,133
You will continue alone for the rest of
the road.

939
01:44:39,150 --> 01:44:41,300
I have always been alone, Osman Bey.

940
01:44:41,660 --> 01:44:45,110
Until I met you and your friends.

941
01:44:45,837 --> 01:44:47,287
Thank you.

942
01:44:47,672 --> 01:44:49,312
Have a nice trip.

943
01:44:49,427 --> 01:44:50,917
But don't forget that...

944
01:44:51,120 --> 01:44:54,250
... you are always welcomed in my tribe,
in my table.

945
01:44:54,455 --> 01:44:56,565
As you say.

946
01:44:57,185 --> 01:44:58,735
Thank you.

947
01:44:58,743 --> 01:45:02,062
Mashallah!

948
01:45:24,599 --> 01:45:27,319
I want to give you this so you can
continue to practice...

949
01:45:31,007 --> 01:45:32,737
...in İznik.

950
01:45:45,385 --> 01:45:47,015
You are very kind.

951
01:45:48,292 --> 01:45:50,022
I hope we will see each other again.

952
01:45:52,694 --> 01:45:54,094
I hope.

953
01:45:58,471 --> 01:45:59,881
The Söğüt Market.

954
01:46:00,123 --> 01:46:02,265
I can't wait to open it.

955
01:46:02,265 --> 01:46:03,861
Those days are close.

956
01:46:03,861 --> 01:46:07,671
But be careful on the road.
The caravan will have arrived before you.

957
01:46:09,395 --> 01:46:11,605
Take care.

958
01:46:53,757 --> 01:46:55,797
We hosted our friend.

959
01:46:57,502 --> 01:46:59,702
Now we reached our goal.

960
01:47:00,228 --> 01:47:01,608
Now...

961
01:47:01,907 --> 01:47:04,247
...now it is time to conquer.

962
01:47:04,977 --> 01:47:06,527
Let's go alps!

963
01:48:03,238 --> 01:48:06,118
Ma'am, I think we arrived.

964
01:48:07,402 --> 01:48:09,342
What if he is not here?

965
01:48:12,806 --> 01:48:14,216
Jesus Christ.

966
01:48:14,624 --> 01:48:16,574
Help us.

967
01:48:16,589 --> 01:48:18,619
Turgut will come, Kornelia.

968
01:48:19,650 --> 01:48:21,550
He won't leave me alone.

969
01:48:40,786 --> 01:48:42,016
Mari.

970
01:48:57,873 --> 01:49:02,983
Smile a bit, Mari.
You are marrying to a noble Lord.

971
01:49:15,520 --> 01:49:17,040
Here we go.

972
01:49:25,133 --> 01:49:27,113
Ambush!
Shield!

973
01:49:28,414 --> 01:49:30,054
Mari stay behind me!

974
01:49:43,070 --> 01:49:44,800
Forward!

975
01:49:45,438 --> 01:49:46,958
Forward!

976
01:49:59,199 --> 01:50:01,139
Turgut!

977
01:50:06,850 --> 01:50:08,550
Stop alps!

978
01:50:19,503 --> 01:50:21,013
Damn it.

979
01:50:29,293 --> 01:50:31,493
I am not going to kill you today, Kosses.

980
01:50:32,848 --> 01:50:35,426
But I wouldn't move if I were you!

981
01:50:35,426 --> 01:50:37,136
I'd stand there!

982
01:50:41,052 --> 01:50:45,372
My archers will kill everyone who moves!

983
01:50:47,661 --> 01:50:49,651
Whoever they are!

984
01:50:50,328 --> 01:50:52,038
Turgut!

985
01:50:59,361 --> 01:51:00,717
Are you crazy?

986
01:51:00,717 --> 01:51:04,767
I am leaving. I told you not to force me!

987
01:51:07,143 --> 01:51:09,733
What are you doing?
Never!

988
01:51:09,821 --> 01:51:13,171
I will never let you go to a Turk!

989
01:51:19,999 --> 01:51:22,009
Then kill me.

990
01:51:31,023 --> 01:51:32,823
What is happening there?

991
01:51:33,027 --> 01:51:35,047
What is happening there?

992
01:51:36,804 --> 01:51:38,344
Mair.

993
01:51:40,797 --> 01:51:43,427
You can't do this to me, Mari.

994
01:51:45,340 --> 01:51:47,410
You'll regret this.

995
01:51:49,202 --> 01:51:50,782
Mari!

996
01:52:01,352 --> 01:52:03,542
The marriage game is over, brother.

997
01:52:21,274 --> 01:52:22,604
Mari!

998
01:52:24,470 --> 01:52:25,890
Alps!

999
01:52:32,863 --> 01:52:35,663
What are you looking for?
Go after them!

1000
01:52:38,639 --> 01:52:40,396
Turgut Bey!

1001
01:52:40,396 --> 01:52:44,276
I have soldiers all around the forest!
You can't run away!

1002
01:53:09,562 --> 01:53:11,362
- Boran.
- My Bey.

1003
01:53:12,153 --> 01:53:14,603
Attack in the middle with alps.

1004
01:53:16,062 --> 01:53:18,162
Then meet our men inside.

1005
01:53:18,387 --> 01:53:19,947
As you order my Bey.

1006
01:53:21,115 --> 01:53:23,195
- Goktug.
- Yes my Bey.

1007
01:53:23,225 --> 01:53:25,325
You'll attack in the right side.

1008
01:53:25,430 --> 01:53:26,760
I'll be on the left.

1009
01:53:26,760 --> 01:53:28,220
Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

1010
01:53:29,418 --> 01:53:31,678
It's time to slaughter!

1011
01:53:40,162 --> 01:53:41,592
However...

1012
01:53:41,902 --> 01:53:44,552
...we can't give any martyr.

1013
01:53:47,050 --> 01:53:50,930
Even one loss means defeat.

1014
01:53:57,007 --> 01:53:58,747
They can't get away.

1015
01:54:05,075 --> 01:54:06,785
They can't get away.

1016
01:54:07,300 --> 01:54:09,030
Turgut!

1017
01:54:09,212 --> 01:54:11,473
I'll make a chalice out of your skull!

1018
01:54:11,473 --> 01:54:12,773
A chalice!

1019
01:54:14,436 --> 01:54:16,236
Hurry Nikola!

1020
01:54:17,551 --> 01:54:19,091
Seperate!

1021
01:54:41,346 --> 01:54:43,046
Come on my lions!

1022
01:54:44,738 --> 01:54:47,308
My Bey, leave.
We'll hold them.

1023
01:55:18,006 --> 01:55:20,086
Let's go Mari.

1024
01:55:55,334 --> 01:55:58,134
Sir, we found this.

1025
01:55:59,619 --> 01:56:01,269
This is Mari's dress.

1026
01:56:04,843 --> 01:56:06,243
Mari.

1027
01:56:08,255 --> 01:56:11,565
Smell, smell, come on.

1028
01:56:12,208 --> 01:56:14,178
Which way?

1029
01:56:16,365 --> 01:56:18,615
Come on, come on, come on.

1030
01:56:19,270 --> 01:56:21,670
Come on boy!
Come on!

1031
01:56:25,587 --> 01:56:27,107
Take us to them!

1032
01:57:07,610 --> 01:57:08,980
Let's go.

1033
01:57:23,892 --> 01:57:25,312
Alps.

1034
01:57:26,083 --> 01:57:28,043
The conquer of Inegol...

1035
01:57:28,557 --> 01:57:30,657
...starts in that mine.

1036
01:57:35,707 --> 01:57:37,467
May our war be holy.

1037
01:57:37,903 --> 01:57:39,213
Go!

1038
01:57:44,573 --> 01:57:46,293
Allah is eternal!

1039
01:57:54,514 --> 01:57:56,504
Attack alps!

1040
01:58:11,116 --> 01:58:12,796
Now!

1041
01:58:29,691 --> 01:58:32,171
The favor of the creator!

1042
01:58:33,260 --> 01:58:34,950
They are here brother.

1043
01:58:37,242 --> 01:58:39,932
- We shall begin then.
- We do, brother.

1044
01:59:52,595 --> 01:59:54,697
They are catching up!

1045
01:59:54,697 --> 01:59:56,860
Where are we supposed to go in this
huge forest?

1046
01:59:56,860 --> 01:59:59,410
Calm down.
I'll not let them hurt you.

1047
02:00:01,407 --> 02:00:02,887
Let's go.

1048
02:00:04,708 --> 02:00:06,058
They are catching up.

1049
02:00:06,719 --> 02:00:08,949
Let them catch up.
I thought of something.

1050
02:00:12,369 --> 02:00:13,869
Get in.

1051
02:00:25,347 --> 02:00:27,037
Check everywhere!

1052
02:00:27,179 --> 02:00:28,699
Everywhere!

1053
02:00:38,159 --> 02:00:39,709
Get away from there!

1054
02:00:43,711 --> 02:00:45,521
I found you Turgut!

1055
02:01:01,827 --> 02:01:03,147
Soldier!

1056
02:01:06,980 --> 02:01:08,720
I found you Turgut!

1057
02:01:08,832 --> 02:01:10,242
I found you!

1058
02:01:10,268 --> 02:01:14,158
I'll let those wolves who you love
so much eat you!

1059
02:01:15,453 --> 02:01:18,693
I'll make a chalice out of your skull!

1060
02:01:18,933 --> 02:01:21,243
I will drink your blood with it!

1061
02:01:22,577 --> 02:01:23,747
Hold on.

1062
02:01:26,930 --> 02:01:29,090
Nikola, Mari.

1063
02:01:44,590 --> 02:01:47,120
Mari is mine!
She is mine!

1064
02:02:35,856 --> 02:02:37,716
Give it to me, brother!

1065
02:02:38,672 --> 02:02:40,362
Hay Masha Allah! (praise be)

1066
02:02:40,849 --> 02:02:42,709
Hay Masha Allah! (praise be)

1067
02:02:43,850 --> 02:02:45,460
Hay Masha Allah! (praise be)

1068
02:02:46,196 --> 02:02:47,696
Hay Masha Allah! (praise be)

1069
02:02:54,208 --> 02:02:55,958
Hay Masha Allah! (praise be)

1070
02:03:13,478 --> 02:03:15,558
Masha Allah(praise be) my valiants!

1071
02:03:55,445 --> 02:03:57,235
Thank Allah my Bey.

1072
02:03:57,889 --> 02:03:59,139
Thank Allah.

1073
02:03:59,649 --> 02:04:01,049
Thank Allah.

1074
02:04:05,672 --> 02:04:08,092
We shall meet our valiant alps...

1075
02:04:08,115 --> 02:04:10,465
who paved the way for...

1076
02:04:10,784 --> 02:04:13,114
...this victory.

1077
02:04:15,918 --> 02:04:17,998
They have men in the mine, Lord!

1078
02:04:18,627 --> 02:04:21,627
We should leave.
Osman claimed the mine!

1079
02:04:25,228 --> 02:04:27,718
We are not waiting in vain, Julia.

1080
02:04:34,899 --> 02:04:36,399
Sir.

1081
02:04:37,536 --> 02:04:39,716
Osman will attack the mine.

1082
02:04:44,452 --> 02:04:45,852
What's your plan?

1083
02:04:47,284 --> 02:04:50,694
I will have a great surprise for him,
Rogatus.

1084
02:04:51,372 --> 02:04:53,452
At the moment he enters that mine...

1085
02:04:53,680 --> 02:04:56,120
The field will be hell!

1086
02:04:57,765 --> 02:05:00,615
I will be at the wedding, as you know...

1087
02:05:01,073 --> 02:05:02,423
...so this pleasure...

1088
02:05:04,957 --> 02:05:08,067
...will be yours to watch, Rogatus.

1089
02:05:12,964 --> 02:05:14,834
Osman will not get out of there!

1090
02:05:20,457 --> 02:05:23,187
So these tunnels will blow!

1091
02:05:23,957 --> 02:05:26,697
This is great news!

1092
02:05:44,101 --> 02:05:45,441
Now...

1093
02:05:46,467 --> 02:05:48,037
Come on!

1094
02:05:55,055 --> 02:05:57,895
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

1095
02:05:58,051 --> 02:06:07,921
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

1096
02:06:08,537 --> 02:06:09,847
Now!

1097
02:06:20,907 --> 02:06:22,327
Come on!

1098
02:06:26,415 --> 02:06:28,465
My heart burns!

1099
02:06:31,224 --> 02:06:33,914
Protect us, our Rab(Allah)

1100
02:06:34,667 --> 02:06:36,157
Alps!

1101
02:06:41,447 --> 02:06:43,287
Wait a bit.

1102
02:06:46,897 --> 02:06:48,497
Come on!

1103
02:06:53,226 --> 02:06:54,936
No.

1104
02:07:37,047 --> 02:07:39,747
Once my Bey conquers the mine...

1105
02:07:40,634 --> 02:07:45,504
...I will forge the best catapults!
I will forge the best cannonballs!

1106
02:07:45,794 --> 02:07:48,494
They will hit
Inegol Castle fast and furious!

1107
02:07:49,898 --> 02:07:51,798
Inshallah(if Allah permits)
Davut Agha.

1108
02:07:52,781 --> 02:07:54,981
Kumral Abdal, check that out.

1109
02:07:59,653 --> 02:08:03,243
Two catapults will shoot from here.

1110
02:08:08,337 --> 02:08:11,887
Two will shoot from right here.

1111
02:08:16,659 --> 02:08:20,539
And three catapults will shoot from here.

1112
02:08:20,814 --> 02:08:23,324
Then the feast will start!

1113
02:08:24,282 --> 02:08:26,352
You just destroy.

1114
02:08:27,043 --> 02:08:29,383
Hit there!
Destroyed here!

1115
02:08:30,110 --> 02:08:33,110
You'll crash down the castle!

1116
02:08:33,270 --> 02:08:35,140
What will my Bey own then?

1117
02:08:38,873 --> 02:08:40,673
Davut Agha.

1118
02:08:40,834 --> 02:08:43,024
The thing is taking it in one piece.

1119
02:08:43,419 --> 02:08:45,249
Not destroying the whole meal.

1120
02:08:46,930 --> 02:08:49,020
Debris is not useful.

1121
02:08:49,511 --> 02:08:53,711
The thing is to have it in one piece
if possible, Master Davut.

1122
02:08:54,365 --> 02:08:59,375
Kumral Abdal, repelling an attack coming
from only one point is easy.

1123
02:08:59,662 --> 02:09:01,978
We'll lose many alps.

1124
02:09:01,978 --> 02:09:04,538
Is the building more important than
our lives?

1125
02:09:04,546 --> 02:09:08,126
Just keep being a saint!

1126
02:09:08,151 --> 02:09:09,891
You have no place in war!

1127
02:09:09,918 --> 02:09:12,656
You are wasting!

1128
02:09:12,656 --> 02:09:15,247
You'll have to repair all those walls!

1129
02:09:15,247 --> 02:09:18,167
I will do it!
I will do it!

1130
02:09:18,416 --> 02:09:20,676
As long as we conquer Inegol.

1131
02:09:22,775 --> 02:09:25,215
Inegol is nothing!

1132
02:09:25,379 --> 02:09:28,019
It is nothing for us!

1133
02:09:29,289 --> 02:09:34,352
We are going to have the
whole world, Davut Agha! The universe!

1134
02:09:34,981 --> 02:09:39,421
All is our homeland, all is ours!

1135
02:09:39,507 --> 02:09:41,947
Allah Allah!

1136
02:09:46,726 --> 02:09:48,446
Kumral Abdal, what's it?

1137
02:09:49,482 --> 02:09:51,332
I felt it.

1138
02:09:53,022 --> 02:09:55,362
I felt something.

1139
02:09:55,949 --> 02:09:58,669
There's something wrong.

1140
02:10:03,589 --> 02:10:05,469
My Allah, protect us.

1141
02:10:56,632 --> 02:10:58,142
My Bey!

1142
02:11:11,282 --> 02:11:12,762
Alps.

1143
02:11:20,129 --> 02:11:21,969
Alps!

1144
02:11:38,456 --> 02:11:40,246
My alps!

1145
02:12:04,838 --> 02:12:06,948
My alps!

1146
